# The premise of `abstract ComputePAC` in every other PAC job, that the
# model's PAC algorithm is a function of its four arguments, spot-checked
# (verus/seams/sys-pac-sign.md, part 3): `pacda x0, x1` with ComputePAC
# unfolded, on concrete operands, key and PC (run.sh section 6, eight
# inputs), so the only symbols left in the trace are the model's
# undefined values and the initial contents of RC, ComputePAC's
# round-constant array. Copies `a` and `b` run the same trace, each with
# its own such symbols, and get the same result, which differs from the
# pointer (the PAC is applied). run.sh prepends the copy and insn lines
# and substitutes @P@ (the pointer).
writes R0 RC
no-mem-write
mem-reads 0
flags-preserved
assert (= a.final.R0 b.final.R0)
assert (not (= a.final.R0 @P@))
